==========================================================================
  LESSON 6 - AIR-GAPPED AI FOR EVERYONE
  Build your own private AI that runs on a laptop with no internet
  BSides Bournemouth 2026
==========================================================================

  This lesson builds a local AI assistant using Ollama and one Python
  script (rag_local_reduced.py). The script downloads information about
  UK university computing, cyber security and IT courses, then the AI
  answers questions from that data - with sources - fully offline.

  HOW IT WORKS

      Build online  -->  Cut the network  -->  Ask questions offline


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  SPECS USED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

                  CLOUD (build)            LOCAL VM (demo)
  OS              Ubuntu 24.04             Ubuntu 24.04 Desktop
  CPU             2 vCPU                   4 vCPU
  RAM             2 GB (+8 GB swap)        8 GB
  Data            590 pages (full)         8 pages (reduced)
  Internet        Yes                      No - air-gapped

  Models:  gemma3:4b (chat)  |  gemma3:1b (light chat)  |  embeddinggemma (search)
  No GPU needed - everything runs on the CPU.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  STEP 1 - UPDATE THE SYSTEM
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

    sudo apt update && sudo apt full-upgrade -y && sudo apt autoremove -y

  Note: Always patch first.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  STEP 2 - CHOOSE YOUR MODEL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

    https://huggingface.co
    https://ollama.com/library

  Note: 1B-4B models run well on a laptop. 7B+ needs more memory.
        Check the training cutoff - it knows nothing after that date.
        Check the licence.
        Uncensored versions exist - safety guardrails removed.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  STEP 3 - INSTALL OLLAMA
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

    curl -fsSL https://ollama.com/install.sh | sh
    ollama --version
    systemctl status ollama --no-pager

  Note: Ollama is the engine that runs the AI. Should say active (running).


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  STEP 4 - SECURITY CHECK
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

    ss -ltnp | grep 11434

  Note: Must show 127.0.0.1:11434 - localhost only, not the network.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  STEP 5 - ADD SWAP (low-memory machines only, around 2 GB RAM)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

    sudo fallocate -l 8G /swapfile && sudo chmod 600 /swapfile
    sudo mkswap /swapfile && sudo swapon /swapfile
    echo '/swapfile none swap sw 0 0' | sudo tee -a /etc/fstab


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  STEP 6 - DOWNLOAD THE MODELS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

    ollama pull gemma3:4b
    ollama pull embeddinggemma
    ollama list

  Note: gemma3:4b writes the answers (~3 GB).
        embeddinggemma finds the right data (~600 MB).
        The ID in "ollama list" is the model's fingerprint.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  STEP 7 - TRY THE MODEL WITHOUT RAG
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

    ollama run gemma3:4b "What is the best UK university for Computer Science?"

  Note: Answers from memory only. No sources. Can be out of date.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  STEP 8 - SET UP PYTHON
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

    sudo apt install -y python3.12-venv python3-pip
    python3 -m venv ~/llm-rag/venv
    source ~/llm-rag/venv/bin/activate
    pip install requests beautifulsoup4 lxml ollama qdrant-client pypdf

  Note: Only needed once.
        After a reboot, run the "source" line again.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  STEP 9 - BUILD THE RAG (online)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

    python3 rag_local_reduced.py sources
    python3 -u rag_local_reduced.py build

  Note: The only step that uses the internet.
        Downloads 8 pages and indexes them - takes a few minutes.
        Respects each site's robots.txt.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  STEP 10 - AIR-GAP IT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

    VMware:  VM > Settings > Network Adapter > untick "Connected"

    ip route
    ping -c 2 8.8.8.8

  Note: ip route is empty and ping fails = no way out.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  STEP 11 - ASK QUESTIONS (offline)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

  With your data (RAG):

    python3 rag_local_reduced.py ask "What is the best UK university for Computer Science?"

  Without your data (bare model), to compare:

    python3 rag_local_reduced.py ask "What is the best UK university for Computer Science?" --no-rag

  Keep asking, one question after another:

    python3 rag_local_reduced.py chat

  Note: The first answer takes a while to start while the model loads.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  STEP 12 - WEB INTERFACE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

    python3 rag_local_reduced.py serve

    Open Firefox:  http://127.0.0.1:8080

  Note: Tick / untick "Use my data (RAG)" to compare answers.
        Use the model dropdown to switch models.
        Ctrl+C in the terminal to stop.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  USEFUL COMMANDS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

    python3 rag_local_reduced.py info       Show models and how much data is loaded
    python3 rag_local_reduced.py reset      Delete the search database (downloads kept)

    CHAT_MODEL=gemma3:1b python3 rag_local_reduced.py chat      Use a different model


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  SECURITY NOTES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

  - Every downloaded page is saved with its source URL and a SHA-256 fingerprint.
  - Ollama and the web page listen on localhost only.
  - Encrypt the disk - the search database is a copy of your data.
  - An air gap stops data leaving, but not bad data going in.
    Review what you feed it (prompt injection).


